2,"Songhay, Koyraboro Senni Language... | Ethnologue Free",https://www.ethnologue.com/language/ses/,Koyraboro Senni Songhay is a stable indigenous language of Mali. It belongs to the Nilo-Saharan language family. The language is used as a first language by all in the ethnic community.,"Songhay, Koyraboro Senni",Nilo-Saharan
3,"Songhay, Koyraboro Senni language resources | Joshua Project",https://joshuaproject.net/languages/ses,"Listing of people groups speaking Songhay, Koyraboro Senni. Songhay, Koyraboro Senni dialects and alternate names. Bible and ministry resource availability.","Songhay, Koyraboro Senni",Nilo-Saharan
4,Songhay,https://languagesgulper.com/eng/Songhay.html,"If they belong to Nilo-Saharan they would be the westernmost family of the phylum.3)Eastern Songhay or Koyraboro Senni. This is the standard Songhay in Mali. Along Niger River from east of Timbuktu, through Bourem and Gao, up to the Mali-Niger border.","Songhay, Koyraboro Senni",Nilo-Saharan
5,Glottolog 5.3 - Koyraboro Senni Songhai,https://glottolog.org/resource/languoid/id/koyr1242,"Songhay, Koyraboro Senni (ses-ses) = 5 (Developing). Recognized language (1982, Decree No. 159 of 19 July, Article 1). Glottocode: koyr1242.","Songhay, Koyraboro Senni",Nilo-Saharan
6,Nilo-Saharan Languages - SourceWatch,https://www.sourcewatch.org/index.php/Nilo-Saharan_Languages,"Nilo-Saharan Languages are a family of 205 languages. The most common are Dholuo in Kenya and Kanuri in Nigeria with 3.5 million speakers each.Songhay, Koyraboro Senni (Mali). Zarma (Niger).","Songhay, Koyraboro Senni",Nilo-Saharan
